From 91eccbd2090aa306f19e83d3341d899cb74c2551 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garrett Brown <themagnificentmrb@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:57:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [capture] Preserve floating-point GLES framebuffer samples

Read floating-point color attachments as floats and normalize them into
the existing 16-bit image pipeline. Keep the previous buffer on readback
failure.

[Hades: merged with the floating-point read Hades had for the half-float
output of nvidia-drm and the picture of native Dolby Vision output, which
this replaces. The one difference left: a floating-point framebuffer is
read in bands of 64 rows, so that its copy in floats stays small (a
3840x2160 picture would take 133 MB at once).]
(cherry picked from commit fda87f10e99d10a64ae679cff83ed0d133ec609d)
